## Solution

**Answer-leak check:** The problem statement contains no solutions, answer values, or proof sketches. Proceeding.

### Setup

We are given
$$f(x,\theta)=\log\!\frac{\Gamma(x+1)}{\Gamma(x+\theta)}-\log\!\left(x+\tfrac{\theta}{2}\right)^{1-\theta}.$$

We want $f\!\left(2,\tfrac13\right)$, i.e. $x=2,\ \theta=\tfrac13$.

### Evaluate each piece

**Gamma ratio.** With $x=2,\ \theta=\tfrac13$:
$$\frac{\Gamma(x+1)}{\Gamma(x+\theta)}=\frac{\Gamma(3)}{\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac73\right)}.$$

$\Gamma(3)=2!=2$. For the denominator, use $\Gamma(z+1)=z\,\Gamma(z)$ repeatedly:
$$\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac73\right)=\tfrac43\,\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac43\right)=\tfrac43\cdot\tfrac13\,\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)=\tfrac49\,\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right).$$

Hence
$$\frac{\Gamma(3)}{\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac73\right)}=\frac{2}{\tfrac49\,\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)}=\frac{9}{2\,\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)},$$
and
$$\log\frac{\Gamma(3)}{\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac73\right)}=\log 9-\log 2-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right).$$

**Power term.** With $x=2,\ \theta=\tfrac13$:
$$\left(x+\tfrac{\theta}{2}\right)^{1-\theta}=\left(2+\tfrac16\right)^{2/3}=\left(\tfrac{13}{6}\right)^{2/3},$$
so
$$\log\!\left(\tfrac{13}{6}\right)^{2/3}=\tfrac23\log\!\tfrac{13}{6}=\tfrac23(\log 13-\log 6).$$

### Combine

$$f\!\left(2,\tfrac13\right)=\bigl(\log 9-\log 2-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)\bigr)-\tfrac23(\log 13-\log 6).$$

Expanding $\log 9=2\log 3$ and $\log 6=\log 2+\log 3$:

$$f=2\log 3-\log 2-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)-\tfrac23\log 13+\tfrac23\log 2+\tfrac23\log 3$$

$$=\tfrac83\log 3-\tfrac13\log 2-\tfrac23\log 13-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)$$

$$=\tfrac13\bigl(8\log 3-\log 2-2\log 13\bigr)-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)$$

$$=\tfrac13\log\!\frac{3^{8}}{2\cdot 13^{2}}-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)=\tfrac13\log\!\frac{6561}{338}-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right).$$

### Numerical value

Using $\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)\approx 2.6789385347077476$:

- $\tfrac13\log\!\tfrac{6561}{338}=\tfrac13\log(19.41124260\ldots)\approx 0.9886174713$,
- $\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)=\log(2.6789385347\ldots)\approx 0.9854206469$.

Therefore
$$f\!\left(2,\tfrac13\right)\approx 0.9886174713-0.9854206469\approx 0.00319682.$$

### Result

$$\boxed{\,f\!\left(2,\tfrac13\right)=\tfrac13\log\!\frac{6561}{338}-\log\Gamma\!\left(\tfrac13\right)\approx 0.00319682\,}$$

